.TH SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_RAW_KEYBOARD_INPUTSINK 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_RAW_KEYBOARD_INPUTSINK \- A variable controlling whether the RIDEV_INPUTSINK flag is set when enabling Windows raw keyboard events.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_RAW_KEYBOARD_INPUTSINK \(dqSDL_WINDOWS_RAW_KEYBOARD_INPUTSINK\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This enables the window to still receive input even if not in foreground\[char46]
.PP
Focused windows that receive text input will still prevent input events from triggering\[char46]
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Input is not received when not in focus or foreground\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Input will be received even when not in focus or foreground\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]4\[char46]

